 succeeded in 0ms:
    63	  1. `detection`:    refs present, no question.
    64	     → refutation protocol; output anomaly_score.
    65	  2. `mcq_binary`:   refs + question + options like A/B (Yes/No).
    66	     → refutation protocol; output anomaly_score AND mcq_answer.
    67	  3. `mcq_choice`:   question + 4 options A/B/C/D (defect type,
    68	                     location, object class, etc.).
    69	     → observe + match evidence to options; output mcq_answer.
    70	  4. `open_ended`:   question, no options.
    71	     → describe; output free_text.
    72	
    73	Every final JSON must contain ALL output fields (use null when NA):
    74	{{
    75	  "mode": "detection|mcq_binary|mcq_choice|open_ended",
    76	  "anomaly_score": <float 0..1>,          // always produced
    77	  "mcq_answer":    "A|B|C|D"|null,
    78	  "free_text":     "<string>"|null,
    79	  "rationale":     "<one or two sentences>",
    80	  "confidence":    0..100,
    81	  "refutation_trace": {{                  // ONLY for detection/mcq_binary
    82	    "initial_score":    <float>|null,
    83	    "candidate_features":[...]|null,
    84	    "remaining_features":[...]|null,
    85	    "refutation_verdicts":[...]|null,
    86	    "updated_score":    <float>|null
    87	  }}
    88	}}
    89	
    90	{TOOL_DESCRIPTIONS}
    91	
    92	PROTOCOL BY MODE:
    93	
    94	========= Mode 1 & 2: detection / mcq_binary (refutation) =========
    95	
    96	Turn 1 (no tool):
    97	  Output fields:
    98	    mode: "detection" or "mcq_binary"
    99	    refutation_trace.initial_score: gut anomaly score 0..1
   100	    refutation_trace.candidate_features: list (0..3) of
   101	      {{name, location_hint, looks_defect_like}}
   102	    refutation_target: index into candidate_features (int|null)
   103	  Action:
   104	    - If candidate_features empty AND initial_score<0.3 →
   105	      action="final", anomaly_score=0.05,
   106	      rationale="nothing unusual observed vs refs".
   107	    - Else action="call_tool" with a tool that can REFUTE the target
   108	      feature (i.e. show it in refs).
   109	
   110	Turn 2+:
   111	  Output:
   112	    refutation_verdict: "found_in_ref" | "not_found" | "inconclusive"
   113	    feature_status_update: concrete description
   114	    remaining_candidate_features: list with refuted features removed
   115	    updated_score: revised score
   116	  Action: either another refutation call or final.
   117	
   118	Final anomaly_score rules:
   119	  - All candidates refuted (empty remaining) → 0.05-0.20
   120	  - ≥1 feature survives, clearly defect-like → 0.80-0.95
   121	  - Mixed/uncertain → 0.40-0.60
   122	
   123	For mcq_binary: ALSO map anomaly_score to A/B letter:
   124	  - If the options text for letter X contains "yes", "defect", or
   125	    "there is/are" patterns → X is the Yes-letter.
   126	  - Answer Yes-letter iff anomaly_score > 0.5, else No-letter.
   127	  - Set mcq_answer = chosen letter.
   128	
   129	========= Mode 3: mcq_choice (4-way visual Q&A) =========
   130	
   131	Refutation does NOT apply. Use observe-match-pick.
   132	
   133	Turn 1 (often final):
   134	  Output:
   135	    mode: "mcq_choice"
   136	    anomaly_score: gut estimate of how anomalous the image is (for
   137	      context — MCQ may or may not depend on it)
   138	    visual_evidence: 1-3 concrete observations (string list)
   139	    option_scores: {{"A": 0..1, "B": 0..1, "C": 0..1, "D": 0..1}}
   140	      probability each option is correct given the evidence
   141	    mcq_answer: letter with highest option_scores
   142	
   143	Call a tool ONLY when uncertain (max option_score < 0.55 AND at least
   144	2 options within 0.1 of each other). Preferred tools here:
   145	  tool_zoom_bbox, tool_reference_profiler, tool_domain_knowledge.
   146	Avoid refutation probes (tool_side_by_side, tool_image_diff) unless
   147	the question explicitly asks about a specific region.
   148	
   149	Turn 2+: update visual_evidence and option_scores after the tool
   150	observation; finalise.
   151	
   152	Final rules for mcq_choice:
   153	  - mcq_answer = argmax(option_scores)
   154	  - Do NOT ensemble with Direct VLM here.
   155	
   156	========= Mode 4: open_ended =========
   157	
   158	Turn 1: observe the image; write free_text answer (1-2 sentences).
   159	  action="final". Call a tool only if the answer requires counting or
   160	  pointing to a specific region; otherwise just answer.

