     1	"""Per-domain active self-evolution experiment.
     2	
     3	Protocol per domain:
     4	  1. Passive eval: run v9 agent on test items → baseline AUROC.
     5	  2. Oracle selection: from DEV split (not test), pick K items with
     6	     highest uncertainty (|agent_score - 0.5|) weighted by
     7	     agent/direct disagreement.
     8	  3. Oracle query: obtain GT labels for those K items (from manifest).
     9	  4. Build per-domain RAG keyed by DINOv2 CLS embedding of query image.
    10	  5. Active eval: re-run v9 on test items with top-3 labelled neighbors
    11	     injected as few-shot context in turn-1 user message.
    12	  6. Report per-domain AUROC Δ.
    13	
    14	Output: one JSON per domain with pre/post scores, plus combined summary.
    15	
    16	Usage:
    17	  python benchmark/scripts/active_learning.py \
    18	    --manifest_dir benchmark/manifests_v2 \
    19	    --domain D1 \
    20	    --output benchmark/results/al_q35_D1.json \
    21	    --k 10 --backend qwen3
    22	"""
